#: docs/explanation/source-map.md:40
msgid ""
"顶层共享 MCU `drivers/` 已归入 F4，不增加运行时转发。ILI9341、XPT2046、W25 继续通过公共 I/O "
"访问设备，留在组件目录，不随 MCU 支持包迁移。"
msgstr ""
"Shared MCU sources formerly under root `drivers/` now belong to F4, without "
"extra runtime forwarding. ILI9341, XPT2046 and W25 continue to use public I/O"
" and remain in components rather than moving with the MCU support package."

#: docs/explanation/source-map.md:47
msgid ""
"精确支持见[支持参考](../reference/platforms/support.md)。重构前的目录与执行范围可从 "
"[固定旧源码](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/tree/8e147fc2c812d81ab6596e0d1a6bc8908d30ac18) "
"追溯；旧记录保留原始身份，不建立本次重构的软件候选或实板资格。"
msgstr ""
"See the [support reference](../reference/platforms/support.md) for exact "
"support. Pre-refactor directories and execution scopes remain traceable at "
"the [fixed prior source](https://github.com/X-Gen-"
"Lab/nexus/tree/8e147fc2c812d81ab6596e0d1a6bc8908d30ac18). Old records retain "
"their original identities and do not establish software candidates or "
"physical-board qualification for this refactor."

#: docs/explanation/source-map.md:43
msgid ""
"Board 和 SoC 不再加载本地 Python 插件。默认 Python 工具集中校验事实并生成静态连接； Core "
"`platform_lifecycle.c` 维护整平台启动、停止、回滚与诊断，F4 `drivers/platform_coordinator.c` "
"维护 System 与共享资源的 C 协调。Host C11 工具是可选主机试点，不是固件 C 化或交付前置。实际生成 factory、模型与 ARM "
"产物 各自验证，不能把源码移动视为整条链路已经验收。 Native 必须显式启用测试 scope，不进入生产系列目录或能力聚合表。"
msgstr ""
"Board and SoC packages no longer load local Python plugins. The default "
"Python tool validates facts centrally and generates static connections. Core"
" `platform_lifecycle.c` owns whole-platform startup, stop, rollback and "
"diagnostics; F4 `drivers/platform_coordinator.c` owns System and shared-"
"resource coordination in C. The Host C11 tool is an optional host pilot, not"
" a prerequisite for firmware behavior in C or delivery. Generated factories,"
" models and ARM artifacts each require validation; moving sources does not "
"establish acceptance of the whole path. Native requires explicit test scope "
"and does not enter production family directories or capability aggregates."
